# React Flow render

Follow `packages/app/REACTFLOW_RENDER.md`. The App renders **execution manifests (v2)** with the
graph model: nodes, ports, branches, tunnels, drawn `end` terminals — see `realignment/graph-model.md`.

Non-negotiables:

- Published edges are **data** only. Layout `control` edges are stripped before publish.
- **`if`**, **`parallel`**, **`loop`**, and drawn **`end`** (`end:<controlId>`) are React Flow nodes;
  the App uses one control node component (Kind: if · for each · for · parallel); `end` has no ports.
- Branches are drawn only for **`$ref`** / **`$state`** bindings; resolve producers per C1 (inputs, step
  `as`, loop `item` / `index`, `if` / `parallel` scoped `as`, merge-port `$ref` lists).
- Data branches only; control nodes and steps with ports; no sequence-only connector UI.
- Tunnels (`ecp-tunnel`) outline each control's lists with labelled tones (`then`, `else`, `path N`, loop
  body). Sized after tree layout; not React Flow `parentId`.